From 53d60edd7ada78193db2bfa3d0032f67aae0f414 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mgirom <84082110+mgirom@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 20:35:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] kv-cache: cpca -- a fitted per-head rotation, scale and
 mean in place of the Hadamard

When LLAMA_KV_CODEBOOK names a GGUF of per-layer, per-head matrices, the quantised
KV cache stores keys and values in a data-fitted basis instead of the Hadamard one:
Q and K are multiplied by matched rotations (V^T diag(s) and V^T diag(1/s)), K and V
are centred before the write, and the attention output is un-rotated and re-centred.
The key-side mean shifts every logit of a query equally, so softmax is unchanged;
softmax weights sum to one, so the value mean comes back exactly. The cache shift
un-rotates, re-applies RoPE and re-rotates with the same matrices. Cache layout,
set_rows, flash attention and the quantisation kernels are untouched; the rate is
q4_0's own.

Prototype: selected by environment rather than a context parameter.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
